        "id": 18176,
        "name": "FearLord",
        "username": "FearLord",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/5f8ce5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-01T15:49:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Something I’ve always thought would make for an interesting discussion in the Letters Page (but I’ve never really know which episode exactly to ask it) is why do the super hero teams of Sentinel Comics seem a lot more static than ‘real world’ comics?</p><p>I mean, some Marvel teams like the Avengers or Xmen have been through huge team changes over the years, but I can pretty much sum up the line up changes to the major Sentinel comics teams in a few lines each:</p><p>Freedom 5</p><p>- Line up change (more of a reboot than a change of characters) at the end of the Golden Age</p><p>- Change of name from Freedom 4 when Absolute Zero joins the team (really early)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Prime Wardens</p><p>- Broke up for a few years</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Dark Watch</p><p>- Mr Fixer Joins early after the first 3 form the team</p><p>- Harpy joins the team</p><p>- Nightmist leaves the team</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>South West Sentinels&nbsp;</p><p>- Changed name to Void Guard</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So why are these teams so stable? Did no new creative team come in and want to shake up these decades old line ups?!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:26.552Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
