        "raw": "<p>Something I&rsquo;ve always thought would make for an interesting discussion in the Letters Page (but I&rsquo;ve never really know which episode exactly to ask it) is why do the super hero teams of Sentinel Comics seem a lot more static than &lsquo;real world&rsquo; comics?</p><p>I mean, some Marvel teams like the Avengers or Xmen have been through huge team changes over the years, but I can pretty much sum up the line up changes to the major Sentinel comics teams in a few lines each:</p><p>Freedom 5</p><p>- Line up change (more of a reboot than a change of characters) at the end of the Golden Age</p><p>- Change of name from Freedom 4 when Absolute Zero joins the team (really early)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Prime Wardens</p><p>- Broke up for a few years</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Dark Watch</p><p>- Mr Fixer Joins early after the first 3 form the team</p><p>- Harpy joins the team</p><p>- Nightmist leaves the team</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>South West Sentinels&nbsp;</p><p>- Changed name to Void Guard</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So why are these teams so stable? Did no new creative team come in and want to shake up these decades old line ups?!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
