      {
        "id": 219451,
        "name": "TheBazaarClerk",
        "username": "TheBazaarClerk",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thebazaarclerk/{size}/2156_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-02T12:33:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'd like to hear C&amp;A comment on this, but until then there's my take:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think this is a result of the way the Sentinels franchise was created and developed. Even though the team made efforts to simulate comic-book excentricities and long backstory into the universe, it's still a franchise managed by a small team for some games that is younger than a decade (compare to various teams working on more than 30 titles for multiple decades). So things are bound to be simpler than if Sentinel Comics was a real company, not only teams would've changed more but we'd have way more teams (At least three Freedom 5s working at the same time, with a \"Teen team\" around way before Daybreak).&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:51:46.019Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
