        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I&#39;d like to hear C&amp;A comment on this, but until then there&#39;s my take:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think this is a result of the way the Sentinels franchise was created and developed. Even though the team made efforts to simulate comic-book excentricities and long backstory into the universe, it&#39;s still a franchise managed by a small team for some games that is younger than a decade (compare to various teams working on more than 30 titles for multiple decades). So things are bound to be simpler than if Sentinel Comics was a real company, not only teams would&#39;ve changed more but we&#39;d have way more teams (At least three Freedom 5s working at the same time, with a &quot;Teen team&quot; around way before Daybreak).&nbsp;</p>",
