      {
        "id": 219452,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-07-02T17:29:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The practical answer is probably: the comic books exist in service to the card game.&nbsp; The card game covers the entire era from about the 60's to today.&nbsp; It would be extremely confusing for the Freedom Five to consist of 10 members (e.g. the Fantastic Four have temporarily included Medusa, Luke Cake, She-Hulk, Ms. Marvel, and Ant-Man just off the top of my head).&nbsp; The X-Men alone, counting its spin-offs, has had more members than the entire SotM card game.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:51:46.092Z",
